[{"sha":"b8585e0c8d7a82bdee9f0ed019cf6edb075e41c1","node_id":"C_kwDOTWzRQtoAKGI4NTg1ZTBjOGQ3YTgyYmRlZTlmMGVkMDE5Y2Y2ZWRiMDc1ZTQxYzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jim Liu 宝玉","email":"junminliu@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-11T03:45:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"Jim Liu 宝玉","email":"junminliu@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-11T03:46:36Z"},"message":"feat(slides): create, edit and annotate slides from agent sessions\n\n- Agents write a deck (decks/<name>/deck.json, slides/*.html, assets/) with\n  the new slides skill; slides_check compiles it with the editor's own\n  compiler and slides_import_asset brings images in. The thread shows a\n  slides card for the deck.\n- The Runtime serves the slides editor page per deck through slides.open,\n  with optimistic-concurrency publishing, asset routes and external-change\n  notices (packages/slides). Space lists decks as a slides entry.\n- Desktop and Web open a deck in a workspace tab to preview, edit, present\n  and export PDF, PPTX or HTML.\n- Annotations made in the editor go to the composer as a slide annotations\n  attachment; the harness resolves them into the prompt and resends them\n  when a message is retried. Location labels follow the UI language.\n- packages/slides-runtime holds the editor runtime, adapted from the Claude\n  Slides implementation: fully typed without any, host capabilities read\n  from slidesHost, no analytics or health reporting, and PptxGenJS 3.12.0\n  patched at build time. apps/slides-editor builds the page and the Node\n  compiler used by slides_check; desktop packaging bundles the build.\n- Docs: docs/design/slides, protocol, architecture, product and acceptance\n  updates.","tree":{"sha":"0e0ba01fc711a4b2f87f9aeb3709ecd1ae826804","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JimLiu/baocut/git/trees/0e0ba01fc711a4b2f87f9aeb3709ecd1ae826804"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JimLiu/baocut/git/commits/b8585e0c8d7a82bdee9f0ed019cf6edb075e41c1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned"